## What to deliver

Build and rig the aircraft up operation by operation until each `parts/<part>.png`
matches the brief, the assembled `scene/` previews show the parts fitting together
correctly, and the rig is complete: a wide, flat fuselage carrying two spinning
rotors, with an underslung cannon beneath the nose. The required interface is a
caller-driven **`cannon_pitch`** joint that tilts the cannon up and down about its
mount, plus the two auto **`rotor_left_spin`** and **`rotor_right_spin`** joints
that whirl the rotors. Produce **every** required part and joint; you may add your
own extra parts, joints, or auto-play clips on top, but do not drop or contradict
the required interface. When you are satisfied, stop: the recorded per-part logs
and `rig.json` are your finished submission.
